Discussion

This paper aimed to examine whether an ecological interface reduces cognitive load, even though it improves performance. Therefore, we used the example of HMIs for speed control and tested a conventional speedometer against an ecological distance speedometer. To assess a larger and more valid set of possible situations, we included an ISA system and a 1-back task in our study. The first research question examines whether driving performance is enhanced by using the ecological distance
